### Handy test requests. Works in VS Code (REST Client extension) and IntelliJ.

### List all tasks
GET http://localhost:9080/api/tasks

### Only finished tasks
GET http://localhost:9080/api/tasks?status=DONE

### Get one task
GET http://localhost:9080/api/tasks/1

### Create a task
POST http://localhost:9080/api/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Write README", "description": "Explain how to run the app" }

### Update a task
PUT http://localhost:9080/api/tasks/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Install WebSphere Liberty", "description": "Done!", "status": "DONE" }

### Delete a task
DELETE http://localhost:9080/api/tasks/2

### Validation error (empty title -> 400)
POST http://localhost:9080/api/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "" }

### Health
GET http://localhost:9080/health

### ---------- Step 3: priority, due dates, sorting ----------

### Create a high-priority task with a due date
POST http://localhost:9080/api/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Prepare demo", "priority": "HIGH", "dueDate": "2026-12-01" }

### Only HIGH priority tasks
GET http://localhost:9080/api/tasks?priority=HIGH

### Most urgent first (HIGH -> LOW)
GET http://localhost:9080/api/tasks?sort=priority

### Soonest deadline first (no due date goes last)
GET http://localhost:9080/api/tasks?sort=dueDate

### Combine: unfinished tasks, soonest deadline first
GET http://localhost:9080/api/tasks?status=TODO&sort=dueDate

### Mark the overdue task as done (overdue flag becomes false)
PUT http://localhost:9080/api/tasks/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Install WebSphere Liberty", "status": "DONE", "priority": "HIGH", "dueDate": "2026-10-13" }

### Bad sort value -> 400 with a JSON error
GET http://localhost:9080/api/tasks?sort=banana
